    "content": "Be still,\nBe quiet,\nDon’t make a sound,\nThey will come if you speak out of turn.\nZipped lips,\nStand tall,\nListen to your elders,\nEven if what they say doesn’t make sense,\nEven if it goes against every fiber of your being.\nIf you go against the grain,\nYou’re the black sheep,\nIf you’d rather love than pray,\nThe devil’s keep.\nTraumatized for the Dawn,\nBefore the day begins,\nHaunted by the ghost of tomorrow,\nOf tomorrow’s ”sins”.\nWalk in front of the path,\nOf a hidden gun,\nBoom,\nBetter check the color of their skin,\nOr the flag that they fly,\nOr if their genitalia matches their face.\nBetter check their chromosomes too,\nOr if they back the right kind of blue.\nTwisted hate and twisted words,\nSalute!\nTo the red white and blue.\nIf you’re not patriotic what happens is on you!\nBetter worship someone who may or may not have existed,\nBetter build all of our laws on that instead of those who are here.\nBut god forbid you’re queer.\nYou’ll be erased from history and books burned.\nWars fought for oil and financial gain,\nIf your heart isn’t filled with love for the Bible you’re insane.\nBut if you walk the line.\nIf you don’t speak out of turn.\nIf you put your hand on your heart,\nPledge allegiance to not changing a damn thing because you’ve got it MADE.\nYour life may be a struggle but it was never made worse,\nJust because the shade of your skin,\nOr the god that you believe in,\nOr the love you let in your heart that harms no one.\nThey say the body is a temple,\nI will offer it happiness,\nI will shape it and nurture it in the way that it pleases.\nSo that instead of being haunted by the memory of tomorrow,\nI open my eyes and smile that I have one,\nBecause not everyone gets one.",
